{"name":"Graceful Mint","hex":"#daeed5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"graceful","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having or showing grace in movement, shape, or proportion.","Magnanimous, lacking arrogance or complaint; gracious."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graceful"},{"term":"mint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A building or institution where money (originally, only coins) is produced under government licence.","A vast sum of money;  a large amount of something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To reproduce (coins), usually en masse, under licence.","To invent; to forge; to fabricate; to fashion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gracefulness","blocks":[{"text":"Gracefulness, or being graceful, is the physical characteristic of displaying \"pretty agility\", in the form of elegant movement, poise, or balance. The etymological root of grace is the Latin word gratia from gratus, meaning pleasing. Gracefulness has been described by reference to its being aesthetically pleasing. For example:"},{"text":"Gracefulness is an idea not very different from beauty; it consists of much the same things. Gracefulness is an idea belonging to posture and motion. In both these, to be graceful, it is requisite that there be no appearance of difficulty; there is required a small inflection of the body; and a composure of the parts in such a manner, as not to encumber each other, not to appear divided by sharp and sudden angles. In this ease, this roundness, this delicacy of attitude and motion, it is that all the magic of grace consists, and what is called its je ne sais quoi; as will be obvious to any observer, who considers attentively the Venus de Medicis, the Antinous, or any statue generally allowed to be graceful in an high degree."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Swan_-_Harrold_Country_Park_October_2009_%284061559567%29.jpg/330px-Swan_-_Harrold_Country_Park_October_2009_%284061559567%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gracefulness"},{"title":"Spring green","blocks":[{"text":"Spring green is a color that was traditionally considered to be on the yellow side of green, but in modern computer systems based on the RGB color model is halfway between cyan and green on the color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%D0%97%D2%AF%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82.jpg/330px-%D0%97%D2%AF%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_green"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Ballet-Ballerina-1853.jpg/500px-Ballet-Ballerina-1853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Ballet-Ballerina-1853.jpg/1280px-Ballet-Ballerina-1853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Ballet-Ballerina-1853.jpg/500px-Ballet-Ballerina-1853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Like swans, ballerinas are often used as an examples of gracefulness.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABallet-Ballerina-1853.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg/500px-Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg/1280px-Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Cerisier_d